+## 64-bit build (fork)
+The upstream release is a 32-bit DLL, which only loads in 32-bit editors. This fork adds an `x64` configuration for 64-bit JED-compatible hosts such as [RED](https://github.com/CodaLilitari/RED), whose plug-in host refuses DLLs of a different architecture.
+
+Build it with Visual Studio 2026 (v145 toolset) and the "C++ MFC for latest build tools" component:
+
+```powershell
+msbuild "Source/Light Baker.sln" /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=x64
+```
+
+The DLL is written to `Source/x64/Release/Light Baker.dll`. Copy it into the editor's `plugins` folder (in RED, then use **Plugins ▸ Rescan**).
+
+The `Build x64` GitHub Actions workflow builds the same configuration on every push and checks that the DLL is x64 and exports `JEDPluginLoadStdCall`. Each run uploads the DLL as the `light-baker-x64` artifact.
+
+64-bit specific changes:
+- The host window handle returned by `GetJedWindow` (an `int`) is sign-extended through `LONG_PTR` before use as an `HWND`.
+- The `/EXPORT:JEDPluginLoadStdCall=_JEDPluginLoadStdCall@4` alias is x86-only; x64 has no stdcall name decoration.
+- x64 configurations match Win32 (static MFC/CRT, C++23, compute shaders compiled to `Source/*.cso` for embedding).
+
+Status: the x64 DLL builds in CI but has not yet been tested inside a 64-bit editor.
+
 # Usage
 ## Sun Light (0x2)
 To create a sun, place a light and set flag "0x2" (sun flag). This light controls the sun direction, color and intensity.
